M05_Cathedral_Controller (100287) needs blackhand_cnt > 7 for 506 and
Mission_Complete(true). Only M05_Cathedral_Para_Unit soldiers with
Soldier_ID 8 and 10 re-drop their squad (X5D_CHTroopdrop8/10) on Killed;
the drop-7 minigunner and the transports ("") do not. A Soldier_ID 8 or
10 soldier removed without Killed (an object below the level extents is
deleted with Destroyed only) ended its chain. Losing both chains capped
the count at the kills so far plus any transports shot down, and the
mission could not complete.

Report such a soldier once from Destroyed as a M05_CATHEDRAL_REINFORCE
with its Soldier_ID, guarded by a SAVE_VARIABLE flag on an unused id that
Killed also sets, and not after M05_CATHEDRAL_FREE. The report is a 1 s
delayed custom, which waits on the controller and is discarded when the
level is torn down. The transports' scripted Destroy_Object at frame 280
is not reported. The kill path, the blackhand_cnt < 9 re-drop bound and
the vehicle counter are unchanged.

--- a/Mission05.cpp
+++ b/Mission05.cpp
@@ -6365,6 +6365,7 @@
 DECLARE_SCRIPT(M05_Cathedral_Para_Unit, "Soldier_ID=0:int")
 {
 	bool cathedral_free;
+	bool loss_reported;
 
 	enum{GO_STAR, ATTACK_STAR};
 
@@ -6373,11 +6374,13 @@
 	REGISTER_VARIABLES()
 	{
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( cathedral_free, 1 );
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( loss_reported, 2 );
 	}
 
 	void Created (GameObject * obj)
 	{
 		cathedral_free = false;
+		loss_reported = false;
 
 		ActionParamsStruct params;
 
@@ -6430,6 +6433,7 @@
 
 	void Killed (GameObject * obj, GameObject * killer)
 	{
+		loss_reported = true;
 		if(!cathedral_free)
 		{
 			int soldier_id = Get_Int_Parameter("Soldier_ID");
@@ -6437,6 +6441,22 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	// Vita: Soldier_ID 8 and 10 carry the only re-drop chains. One removed
+	// without Killed (it fell below the level extents) ended its chain and
+	// could cap blackhand_cnt below 8. Report it once like a kill so the
+	// chain continues. The transports (Soldier_ID "") are removed by their
+	// text after every drop and are not reported. The delayed custom waits
+	// on the controller, so a level teardown discards it.
+	void Destroyed (GameObject * obj)
+	{
+		int soldier_id = Get_Int_Parameter("Soldier_ID");
+		if(!loss_reported && !cathedral_free && (soldier_id == 8 || soldier_id == 10))
+		{
+			loss_reported = true;
+			Commands->Send_Custom_Event(obj, Commands->Find_Object(100287), M05_CATHEDRAL_REINFORCE, soldier_id, 1.0f);
+		}
+	}
+
 };
 
 DECLARE_SCRIPT(M05_Cache_Surprise, "")
